Morning Everybody,<P>Was a long, but fruitful night last night.  Sounds like alpha group made some good exp as well.  I managed to ding twice last night, so Rakasak is now level 30 and finally has Flying Kick.  Woot!  The max damage I saw last night after going back to town and putting a training point into it was 52.  The special "move" that Rak does for the FK looks like a flying round kick, not quite as cool as the flying front kick the humans do, but oh well.  Since I got Vowk killed a few times over the weekend, I grouped him with Rak after dinging to 30, and managed to get Vowk to within half a bubble of re-dinging to 29th.  I'm soloing giants, burynai miners, and goblin raiders in FM now, and hoping to get a few more fast levels, any advice for soloing monks at 30'ish is appreciated.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Now, I've got a couple questions that I'm hoping Brod can answer, because I can't seem to find the info anywhere.<P>1.  Is the amount healed by Mend level determined, skill determined, or a fixed percentage?<BR>2.  Is the damage done by Flying Kick level determined, or skill determined?<BR>3.  What kinda AC do you have right now on Brod?  I'm feeling a little "light" in the AC department, and wondering what kinda gear I should be shooting for.<P>Thanks, and take Care<P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 55th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Rakasak Smakatak - 33rd Level Monk<BR>Bertox. Server<P>Wardak - 7th Level Norseman Warrior<BR>Gawaine Server
