<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
<I>1. Is the amount healed by Mend level determined, skill determined, or a fixed percentage?</I><P>If successful, Mend heals 25% of total HP (1.25 bubbles).  Because of that, monks often strive for HP enhancing gear.  Recycle time is 6 minutes real-time.<P><I>2. Is the damage done by Flying Kick level determined, or skill determined?</I><P>I believe the formula for FK damage contains both level and skill.  Around 40th level your FK will start to hit for over 100 sometimes.<P><I>3. What kinda AC do you have right now on Brod? I'm feeling a little "light" in the AC department, and wondering what kinda gear I should be shooting for.</I><P>I'm also light in the AC department (simply because there aren't high AC items that are light), and monks just live their life that way.  Where we kind of make up for that is with Dodge, Block and Riposte.  At 40th level each of those skills will work slightly over 3% of the time, so with the combination of all three you end up avoiding 10% of the hits that would normally damage you.
</FONT>
