Thanks for the answers Brod.  Kinda figured that was how they all worked, but wanted some clarification.  So I guess once mend is over 100 their really is no point in trying to raise the skill beyond that.  Now, my mini-rant about monks since I've played one for 30 levels, and have a couple "issues" with them I wanna get off my chest.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>1.  Minimum damage on special attacks.  Rogues get it on backstabs, why don't monks get a minimum damage?  I noticed that I've never done less than 3 damage with a FK, so maybe that is its minimum, but jesus, a level 30 rogue hits for a minimum of 30 on their BS.  I think a monk should get the same thing, especially since you'll never see a monk do a double flying kick for 1k damage total.<P>2.  Why can't monks "chain" their special attacks?  it's not like they are overpowering in ANY way shape or form, and it would just be cool as hell.  How many hand to hand combatants, not counting the normal boxing types, just stand there and once in awhile throw a kick or sweep?  If a monk could chain their special attacks it would be fun, and be a little extra damage, but not overpowering.  Imagine seeing the monk in your group throw out a Tail Rake, followed by a Flying kick, and then start throwing punches in a flurry.  Would be damn cool.  <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Thats it for now, give me a few more levels, and I'm sure i'll have more to bitch about. :P<P>--------------------<P>Lownar Baardeth - 55th Level Gnecromancer<BR>Kalaan - 30th Level Rogue<BR>Rakasak Smakatak - 33rd Level Monk<BR>Bertox. Server<P>Wardak - 7th Level Norseman Warrior<BR>Gawaine Server
